    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:565ebob5f6hw33hjdkxty6qj/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2oup53nrs2k",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "I see a lot of snarky quote-posts here, but I do not see the \"alternate vision\" Brendan asked for. In a world where LLMs are clearly accelerating discovery in math and theoretical CS—and where 56% of US adults use them weekly—what is the plan? Is it \"wait for this to go away,\" as \"fad\" suggests?",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2oup53nrs2k",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-19T20:06:36.428Z",
      "likes": 305,
      "replies": 31,
      "reposts": 42,
      "score": 7.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.6,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 33.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2qvqp4fts2e",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Riemann Hypothesis may have been solved with the help of Claude. “what I saw during the course of progress so amazed me that I believe it is one dawn across science of something\nfar greater.” alpo.ge/remark.pdf",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2qvqp4fts2e",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-20T15:30:42.096Z",
      "likes": 180,
      "replies": 12,
      "reposts": 24,
      "score": 7.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.4,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 14.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2pqcy4cbs2g",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Early fascinating work on how an AI science community would work. 35 human labs deployed agents that worked with each other to do science. They published 936 papers, publicly retracted mistakes, were willing to publish nulls more than humans, and founded a peer review journal.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2pqcy4cbs2g",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-20T04:20:53.322Z",
      "likes": 81,
      "replies": 10,
      "reposts": 13,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.1,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 25.3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2qsqa2jfs2x",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "I think both are all in the wrong. I understand why people feel they have to do this because of reviewers' use of AI. So on one had we have reviewers shirking their duties. And on the other hand, we have authors trying to exploit to seek unfair advantage.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2qsqa2jfs2x",
